  steps:
    1. Pick N=2-4 frames. Assign each a distinct color from non-black/grey palette
    2. Choose N distinct marker counts in range 2-8
    3. For each frame, pick interior size >= marker count (h>=3, w>=3, h*w >= count+2)
    4. Pick border thickness per side (1-4) to get bbox = interior + borders
    5. Place frames on a 20-25 square grid with non-overlapping bboxes
    6. Fill frame border with its color, interior with bg
    7. Scatter marker-count grey pixels randomly in interior bg cells
    8. Build output: sort frames by marker count ascending, one row per frame
